    "id": "xr_prize_u0_loop_defect_maxwell_rank_one_compiler",
    "title": "XR prize u=0 loop-defect Maxwell and rank-one compiler",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For a prize P-A u=0,v>=1 cell, deleting at most v exceptional slopes and puncturing the global roots gives a coherent GRS_a family with block size a+h+v and pair cap a+v. Every minimal dense core on t blocks has at least v(t-2)+e+1 independent trades. Its rank-one trades are exactly common-support records (S,Q,alpha), where a+1<=|S|<=a+v, deg Q<|S|-a, Q is nonzero on S, and alpha satisfies the two slope parity equations. This is a structural compiler, not an aggregate count.",
